        {
            "id": "32276791",
            "user": "Agusbou2015",
            "timestamp": "16:38, 9 February 2024",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(4,067 bytes)",
            "change": 4053,
            "summary": "(RCP reverted edits by 204.108.126.115 (talk) to  revision #32256539 by ShowierData9978)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "These basic vanilla cupcakes are super easy to make and can be whipped up quickly for a snack. They're a good first time cupcake for a baker who is learning the ropes or for younger children in the kitchen. Since they're plain, you can add any type of frosting you like.",
                    "",
                    "[[Category:Cupcakes]]",
                    "",
                    "==Ingredients ==",
                    "*⅓ cup butter",
                    "*½ cup sugar",
                    "*1 tsp. vanilla extract",
                    "*2 eggs",
                    "*1¼ cups all-purpose flour",
                    "*1¼ teaspoon baking soda",
                    "*¼ cup milk",
                    "== Steps ==",
                    "#Cream together the butter with the sugar until light and moist.<br><br>[[Image:Make Basic Cupcakes Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Add the vanilla extract and mix it in.<br><br>{{whvid|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 2.360p.mp4|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 2-preview.jpg|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 2 Version 2.jpg}}",
                    "#Add the eggs (one at a time) to the batter. Mix it well.<ref>https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/go-to-vanilla-cupcakes-3338835</ref> (It may look like it's curdling but don't worry.)<br><br>{{whvid|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 3.360p.mp4|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 3-preview.jpg|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 3 Version 2.jpg}}",
                    "#Add the flour with the baking soda and milk. Mix well until all bits of flour disappear.<ref>https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/go-to-vanilla-cupcakes-3338835</ref><br><br>{{whvid|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 4.360p.mp4|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 4-preview.jpg|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 4 Version 2.jpg}}",
                    "#Preheat oven to {{convert|350|F|round=5}}.<ref>https://www.eggs.ca/recipes/classic-vanilla-cupcakes</ref>[[Image:Make Basic Cupcakes Step 5 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Line your cupcake pan with cupcake liners.<ref>https://www.taste.com.au/recipes/classic-cupcakes/85286555-6ff1-40cc-a7aa-c8e63cb17933</ref><br><br>{{whvid|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 6.360p.mp4|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 6-preview.jpg|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 6 Version 2.jpg}}",
                    "#Add the batter into the cupcake liners. Fill them half up.<br><br>{{whvid|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 7.360p.mp4|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 7-preview.jpg|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 7 Version 2.jpg}}",
                    "#Bake the cupcakes for 15-20 minutes. Insert a toothpick and if it comes out clean your cupcakes are done.<ref>https://www.bonappetit.com/story/how-to-tell-baked-good-is-done</ref><br><br>{{whvid|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 8.360p.mp4|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 8-preview.jpg|Make Basic Cupcakes Step 8 Version 2.jpg}}",
                    "#*Avoid opening the oven in the middle of the baking process. Do it only when it is time to check if your cupcakes are done.<ref>[v162147_b01]. 26 May 2022.</ref>",
                    "#Let them cool for a few minutes in the pan then take them out.[[Image:Make Basic Cupcakes Step 9 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Serve. Your awesome and delicious cupcakes are done![[Image:Make Basic Cupcakes Step 10 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Frost or ice the cupcakes with your choice of flavored frosting/icing.",
                    "#*Don't frost freshly baked warm cupcakes. Make sure that they are completely cold.<ref>[v162147_b01]. 26 May 2022.</ref>",
                    "#*If you wish, you can even swirl different frostings together as long as they have the same consistence, for example buttercream and chocolate ganache. Or, you can use the same kind of frosting but of different colors. Layer your frostings on a piece of plastic wrap, and then roll it like a sandwich.<ref>[v162147_b01]. 26 May 2022.</ref>",
                    "#*If you wish, you can put some filling inside your cupcakes. Use an apple corer to make the hole in the cupcake, then fill them with whatever you like using a piping bag.<ref>[v162147_b01]. 26 May 2022.</ref>",
                    "",
                    "== Video ==",
                    "{{Video:Make Basic Cupcakes|}}",
                    "",
                    "== Tips ==",
                    "*Add frosting for a delicious ending.",
                    "",
                    "== Warnings ==",
                    "*Supervise children if they are making the cupcakes.",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "== Related wikiHows ==",
                    "*[[Make Quick Easy Cupcakes]]",
                    "*[[Make Cupcakes]]",
                    "",
                    "<!-- Expert Interview code below. Please do not remove. -->",
                    "== Expert Interview ==",
                    "Thanks for reading our article! If you’d like to learn more about cooking, check out our in-depth {{expert_interview_link: wikiHow Expert Interview Transcript Maha Mohamed Part 1 | interview}} with [v162147_b01].",
                    "",
                    "==References==",
                    "{{reflist}}"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "make a cupcake"
                ]
            }
        },
